---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const sections = [
  { id: 'about', title: 'About these terms' },
  { id: 'using-the-site', title: 'Using this website' },
  { id: 'quotes', title: 'Enquiries and quotes' },
  { id: 'projects', title: 'Software and student projects' },
  { id: 'training', title: 'Training courses' },
  { id: 'ownership', title: 'Ownership of content' },
  { id: 'other-services', title: 'Links to other services' },
  { id: 'liability', title: 'Our responsibility to you' },
  { id: 'law', title: 'Governing law' },
  { id: 'contact', title: 'Contact' },
];
const mail = `mailto:${site.email}`;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms of use"
  slug="terms"
  description="The terms that apply when you use The Consultant's website, send an enquiry, commission a project or apply for training."
  lead="The ground rules for using this website, and the general terms behind our projects and training courses."
  updated="2026-09-25"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="about">
    <h2>About these terms</h2>
    <p>
      These terms apply when you use this website or contact The Consultant ("we", "us"), a technology firm based in
      Ghana. By using the site you accept them. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.
    </p>
    <p>
      Work we do for you is also covered by what we agree with you in writing, for example by email or WhatsApp. If
      that written agreement says something different from these terms, the written agreement applies.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="using-the-site">
    <h2>Using this website</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>send false, misleading or someone else's details through our forms;</li>
      <li>send spam, or try to overload, break into or interfere with the site;</li>
      <li>copy the site's content for commercial use without our permission.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We work to keep the information here accurate and the site available, but courses, modules and services change
      over time and the site may occasionally be unavailable.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="quotes">
    <h2>Enquiries and quotes</h2>
    <p>
      Sending a message or an application does not create a contract. Prices, timelines and schedules are confirmed
      with you directly, in writing, before any work or training starts. A quote is based on the information you
      give us; if the scope changes, the price or timeline may change too, and we will agree that with you first.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="projects">
    <h2>Software and student projects</h2>
    <h3>Your part</h3>
    <p>
      You give us accurate requirements, materials and feedback on time, and you confirm you have the right to use
      anything you send us, such as logos, text, data or images.
    </p>
    <h3>Final year and industrial projects</h3>
    <p>
      We support students from proposal to a working, documented system, and we take care that you understand every
      part of it. You remain responsible for following your institution's rules on academic work and for the work you
      submit and defend.
    </p>
    <h3>Who owns the result</h3>
    <p>
      Once a project is paid for in full, you own the finished deliverables made specifically for you, unless we agree
      otherwise in writing. We keep the right to reuse our general know-how, tools and non-confidential building
      blocks. We treat your project information as confidential.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="training">
    <h2>Training courses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Applying does not guarantee a place. We confirm your class, start date, schedule and fees before you begin.</li>
      <li>Fees, payment dates and any refund arrangements are those confirmed to you at enrolment.</li>
      <li>For JHS and SHS learners, a parent or guardian must agree to the enrolment and the fees.</li>
      <li>Learners are expected to attend, take part respectfully and follow the rules of the class, online or in person.</li>
      <li>We may update course content, trainers or schedules to keep training current, and will tell you about changes that affect you.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="ownership">
    <h2>Ownership of content</h2>
    <p>
      The text, design and course material on this site belong to The Consultant or are used with permission. You may
      view and share pages for personal use. Course materials given to you are for your own learning and may not be
      resold or republished.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="other-services">
    <h2>Links to other services</h2>
    <p>
      Some buttons open WhatsApp, and training applications are received through Google Forms. Those services have
      their own terms and privacy policies, and we are not responsible for how they operate. See our{' '}
      <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for what we share with them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="liability">
    <h2>Our responsibility to you</h2>
    <p>
      We provide our services with reasonable care and skill. To the extent Ghanaian law allows, we are not liable for
      indirect losses, such as lost profits or data, arising from use of this website, and our total liability for any
      piece of work is limited to the amount you paid us for it. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under
      Ghanaian law that cannot be limited.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="law">
    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Ghana. If a dispute arises, we will first try to resolve
      it with you directly; if that fails, the courts of Ghana have jurisdiction.
    </p>
    <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The "Last updated" date above shows when they last changed.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms: <a href={mail}>{site.email}</a>, or call
      {site.phones.map((p, i) => <>{i > 0 && ' or '}<a href={`tel:${p.tel}`}>{p.display}</a></>)}.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
